---
import InvestigateLayout from '../layouts/InvestigateLayout.astro';
---

<InvestigateLayout title="OpenVidya">
  <section class="inv-card hero">
    <p class="inv-kicker">Grades 8–12 · Electricity & magnetism</p>
    <h1 class="inv-title">OpenVidya</h1>
    <p class="inv-lead">
      Don’t tell me what happens. Make me commit to what I think will happen.
    </p>
    <p class="inv-lead" style="margin-top:-0.4rem">
      Observe · Compare · Judge · Then model
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="inv-card">
    <p class="inv-kicker">Electricity</p>
    <h2 class="inv-title" style="font-size:1.3rem">Where to start</h2>
    <a class="start-card" href="/learn/electricity/what-is-charge">
      <span class="tag">Investigation · E1</span>
      <strong>What is charge?</strong>
      <span class="desc">
        Predict, try balloons, face a conflict, judge competing explanations — then earn the charge
        model. No particle names. No formula dump.
      </span>
      <span class="go">Begin →</span>
    </a>
    <p class="note-soft">
      You will need two balloons, thread, and dry hair or wool. Commitments lock until you observe.
    </p>

    <a class="start-card next" href="/learn/electricity/what-decides-the-push">
      <span class="tag">Investigation · E2</span>
      <strong>What decides how hard two charges push?</strong>
      <span class="desc">
        E1 showed <em>that</em> charges push. This asks what decides <em>how hard</em> — and ends
        with the honest answer that your own measurement may not be sharp enough to say.
      </span>
      <span class="go">Continue →</span>
    </a>
    <p class="note-soft">
      Needs a bench: eight metal-coated balls, thread, a millimetre ruler, a rubbed rod, and a
      dry day. <strong>Nobody has built this apparatus yet.</strong> The page says so on its first screen. It also tells you what to send back if you do.
    </p>

    <a class="start-card next" href="/learn/electricity/how-does-it-know">
      <span class="tag">Investigation · E3</span>
      <strong>How does one charge know the other is there?</strong>
      <span class="desc">
        Two objects, nothing between them, and a force. E2 never mentioned it — and this one ends
        without settling the question, on purpose.
      </span>
      <span class="go">Continue →</span>
    </a>
    <p class="note-soft">
      Needs nothing at all: no balloons, no bench, no dry day. A pencil and your own judgment.
      That is not a gap in the lesson. Some questions are not settled by measuring harder.
    </p>

    <a class="start-card next" href="/learn/electricity/why-neutral-paper-moves">
      <span class="tag">Investigation · E4</span>
      <strong>Why does a comb pick up paper nobody rubbed?</strong>
      <span class="desc">
        The usual formula says a neutral scrap feels no force. It jumps anyway. Two trials, and
        the second one decides between two stories.
      </span>
      <span class="go">Continue →</span>
    </a>
    <p class="note-soft">
      A dry comb and torn paper. Everything here can actually be done, which is not true of
      E2 yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="inv-card">
    <p class="inv-kicker">Your models</p>
    <p class="inv-lead" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem">
      Models you earn stay available for later investigations.
    </p>
    <a class="inv-btn" href="/models">Open model inventory</a>
  </section>

  <section class="inv-card muted-card">
    <p class="inv-kicker">What comes next</p>
    <p class="note-soft" style="margin-top:0">
      E1 is the first investigation in the electricity sequence. The rest are being built the
      same way — question first, prediction before answer, model last.
    </p>
    <div class="legacy">
      <span>E5 · Why does it take effort to push a charge closer? — planned</span>
    </div>
  </section>
</InvestigateLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    background: linear-gradient(165deg, #eff6ff 0%, #fff 55%);
  }
  .start-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    border: 2px solid #bfdbfe;
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    background: #f8fbff;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }
  .start-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .start-card .tag {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .start-card strong {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
  .start-card .desc {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: #4b5563;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .start-card .go {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .muted-card {
    opacity: 0.95;
  }
  .legacy {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .legacy span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
</style>
